  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFRAH 2023 GRANT PAYMENT FOR PROGRAMME TO END FGM IN SOMALIA AND THE HORN OF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ifrah Foundation was founded in 2010 by Ifrah Ahmed an Irish citizen, originally from Somalia. Ifrah Ahmed is a global campaigner on eliminating FGM and holds the position of Gender Advisor to the Federal Government of Somalia. The Foundation&#x2019;s work aligns with the SDGs, as its goal centres around the development and implementation of a National Action Plan for the Eradication of FGM/C in Somalia by 2030. Additionally, it works to campaign/advocate through media in Somalia, regionally, and globally to end FGM in collaboration with a range of partners including the Global Media Campaign. The Foundation&#x2019;s three primary activities are those of advocacy, awareness raising and community empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
